    <article class="notice-content">
        <h2>About this study</h2>
        <p>E-Waste Connect is a university study of e-waste coordination in Nairobi County. It is not an official county or regulator service. Use synthetic data for evaluation.</p>
        <h2>Information used for account access</h2>
        <p>We store your email, optional display name, a password hash, account status, role and the version and date of your notice acknowledgment. Account information supports sign-in, access control and password recovery. Session cookies maintain your sign-in; recovery links expire after 60 minutes.</p>
        <h2>Access and security</h2>
        <p>Passwords are hashed. Recovery tokens are stored as hashes. Authorized project administrators control staff provisioning. Security records use account identifiers without password or recovery-token contents. Local evaluation recovery messages remain private to the project operator.</p>
        <h2>Evaluation and retention</h2>
        <p>Synthetic data is the default. Any evaluator personal data must be collected with informed permission and removed within 90 days after assessment, following the study retention policy. Account information is used for this study and is not sold.</p>
        <h2>Questions and account information</h2>
        <p>Contact the researcher through the study contact provided with your evaluation invitation about access, correction or deletion. Self-service privacy requests are not yet available. Acknowledging this notice records that you have read it; it does not authorize new uses of your information.</p>
        <p class="hint">Notice version {{ $noticeVersion }} is retained with each Consumer registration.</p>
    </article>
